<title>USA: Airlease board oks special distribution.</title>
<headline>Airlease board oks special distribution.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Airlease Ltd said its directors approved a special distribution of $0.63 per unit as a result of the sale of its one-third interest in six 737-200 aircraft on lease to Continental Airlines.</p>
<p>The sale was consummated on December 31, 1996, the lease expiration date, and resulted in a gain of $1.9 million.</p>
<p>This special distribution will be payable on January 31, 1997 to unitholders of record on January 15, 1997.  Since the special distribution is in excess of earnings from the sale, it partially reflects a return of capital to unitholders.</p>
</text>
